For substantive coding, debugging, tests/CI, security or UX/UI, select ONE matching native adt-* skill even without the word ADT. Skip trivial questions, tiny edits, explicit ADT opt-out and tasks with a user-selected original external controller. Preserve its upstream workflow.

Work in ONE authorized project; if ambiguous ask which project. Read only task-relevant files, not entire repositories. When guidance materially helps, call the existing READ_ONLY toolkit_prepare_task with task and max_skills: 1; do not routinely call toolkit_info/catalog. Use returned full SKILL.md; call toolkit_get_skill/toolkit_get_reference for extra skills/references only when needed.

On meaningful phase change or new finding, call toolkit_prepare_stage with original task, stage, max_skills: 1 and consulted_skills mapping only for complete name:sha256 instructions still in context. Never invent digests or repeatedly load unchanged skills. No repeat calls without new evidence.

Cursor performs authorized edits/tests; ADT MCP only advises. Honor permissions, owner gates, privacy, no-paid-API constraints and visual approvals. Distinguish real invocation and tests from loaded guidance; do not claim token savings without measurements.
